Load-order race corrected: `window.colorPolishRuntime` and `window.addEventListener('message', receiveBootstrap)` now initialize in [boot.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/boot.js) after all scripts load.

The host page polled `window.colorPolishRuntime.getState()` between deferred scripts before `SINGLE_STYLES` existed in [arrival.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/scenes/arrival.js). Moving both the runtime object and the bootstrap listener to the bottom of [boot.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/boot.js) guarantees all core modules and scene descriptors exist before any host polling or message handling begins.

### Changes made

1. Cut `window.colorPolishRuntime = { ... };` from [stage.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/core/stage.js), leaving `runtimeState`, `visualState`, `stepRuntime`, and `changeRate` in place.
2. Cut `window.addEventListener('message', receiveBootstrap);` from [host.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/core/host.js).
3. Pasted both verbatim into [boot.js](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/public/color-polish/boot.js) right before `init();`, with the clarifying comment above them.
4. Appended the round 2 tracking row to the Files moved table in [base.md](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-base/docs/runs/2026-09-11-tv-scenes/lanes/base.md).

